(--- The ledger's file leaves, batch B2, 2026-08-29 night -----------------

 docs/ledger/files.md rows FIL-45, FIL-52, FIL-53, FIL-54, FIL-55, FIL-56,
 FIL-70, FIL-75, FIL-80, FIL-93. Same shared machinery as batch B just
 above: the name allocator, the D16 guard repeated per leaf rather than
 shared, every path built from gen_scratch_flag, every assertion read on
 the still-open handle before any Close. Hand-verified against BOTH
 compilers before being encoded here (0.4.14 installed, and the 0.4.15
 stack) - every probe below produced identical output on each.

 Retained probes: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-45.vox, FIL-53.vox,
 FIL-54.vox, FIL-56.vox, FIL-70.vox, FIL-75.vox, FIL-93.vox already
 existed (hand-verified when their ledger rows were first written) and
 match the shape below exactly; FIL-52 and FIL-80 gained fresh probes
 this batch (docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-52.vox, FIL-80.vox).)

(FIL-45: `Read from ... into ...` REPLACES the buffer's contents rather
 than appending to them - LANGUAGE.md:4001. Pre-seed the sink with a
 known length, `Read` a file of a different known length into it, and
 assert the post-read size is the READ length, not the sum - an
 appending bug would fail this the same way D2's own probe caught it for
 the compiler originally. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-45.vox.)

