(FIL-56: for a fixed-size buffer, an overlong `Read line` is truncated to
 capacity and the error flag is set - LANGUAGE.md:4023. A capacity
 strictly below the line's length, so the truncation is never
 accidental; the size check and the flag check are the same two-part
 shape 'gen leaf buffer fixed overflow' (gen_buffers.vox) uses for the
 equivalent buffer-append claim, reused here rather than copied since a
 file-backed `Read line` truncation and a plain `append` truncation are
 the same underlying rule (LANGUAGE.md:3567) exercised through a
 different statement. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-56.vox.)

