(FIL-80: file operation failures are catchable - LANGUAGE.md:4139-4141.
 The plainest forced failure a generator can guarantee: open a path
 inside its own scratch directory that it never created, for READING
 (writing always succeeds/creates), and confirm `On error` fires. No
 property is read on the failed-open handle afterward and it is never
 `Close`d - both a real fd and a well-defined post-failure state are
 unproven here, and FIL-89/FIL-96 already cover a forgotten `Close`
 being safe. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-80.vox.)

