(FIL-93: on open, the FD is registered in a tracking table, and no
 descriptor is recycled while a handle stays live - LANGUAGE.md:4200.
 The retained probe pushes this to 100000 unclosed opens; a leaf embedded
 among many others in a fuzzed program needs no such scale to put the
 claim on trial, so this draws a modest 5-19 and checks every descriptor
 strictly increasing over the previous one - proof none was recycled
 while all the earlier ones stayed open, the same reasoning at a size
 that keeps program generation and compilation fast. Every open targets
 the SAME already-created file (concurrent read-only opens of one path
 are ordinary and each still gets its own fd), inside a `For each …
 from 1 to N` loop - one period after the loop's last body statement
 closes the loop itself, per LANGUAGE.md's "one period closes one
 level" rule; nothing here needs a stacked period since the inner `If`
 already closed itself first. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-93.vox.)

