(FIL-57, FIL-61, FIL-102, and FIL-63's line-past-EOF sub-case: `Seek
 <file> to line N` is accepted (LANGUAGE.md:4031) and lands on the first
 byte of line N (LANGUAGE.md:4038) - proved by seeking to one drawn line
 of a file built from K lines of distinct known lengths and asserting
 `Read line` returns exactly that line, trailing newline included (the
 same reading FIL-53 already established). A file ending in a newline
 has exactly K newlines, so line K+1 is the one empty trailing line the
 manual documents as existing (LANGUAGE.md:4042-4044): seeking there and
 reading must NOT set the error flag and must return an empty buffer;
 line K+2 is past that and MUST set the error flag - also FIL-63's third
 invalid-target case (the other two are in 'gen leaf file seek invalid
 targets'). Fixed by vox #47 (0.4.8, Discrepancy 3, resolved) - re-hand-
 verified this batch under both compilers. `Seek` was emitted by no leaf
 anywhere in `src/` before this batch. Probes: docs/ledger/probes/files/
 FIL-57.vox, FIL-63.vox, FIL-102.vox, D3.vox.)

