(FIL-09: the File Properties worked example - LANGUAGE.md:3842-3848:
 open for reading, read `size` and `modified`, then guard on `size is
 greater than` a threshold. The size is the payload length the generator
 wrote; `modified` is checked as a range and never printed, for the
 wall-clock reason 'gen file assert range quietly' records; and the
 guard's threshold is drawn so the generator knows which way it goes -
 the manual's own 1048576, which the payload never reaches, the length
 itself or one below it (the boundary from both sides), zero, or any
 'gen extreme number'. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-09.vox.)

