(FIL-15: the List Properties worked example - LANGUAGE.md:3886-3891 - and
 the point it makes: a Boolean property is a condition on its own, `If
 names's empty then,` with no comparison. 'gen assert true'/'false'
 compare (`is false`), so they never put the bare form on trial; here the
 bare form sets a flag and the flag is asserted. The list is empty or
 holds one to five literals of a drawn type, so the guard fires in some
 programs and not in others. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-15.vox.)

