 it keeps holding over several rounds: seed the file, then reopen for
 appending one to five times, each round writing a drawn chunk -
 sometimes zero bytes, a `Write ""` that must leave the size alone - and
 asserting the running size on the live handle; finally read the whole
 file back and assert it is every chunk in order. An append that wrote
 at the start, or truncated on open, fails the content check even where
 the sizes happen to agree. Probe: docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-34.vox.)

